// lenses.cost — symbolic-cost lens over the v3 DAG.
//
// Status: STRUCTURALLY TERMINAL; BEHAVIORALLY COMPLETE
//   (T-CostLens-Composition α-narrow #38 + #39 satisfied by construction at
//   HEAD per PR #2171. **ε path ratified canonical-not-transitional** at
//   gunb-ai/gunbc#2181 #issuecomment-4401584012 (canvas
//   `docs/proposals/q-cost-composition-layering-canvas.md`): cost factors
//   as (target-agnostic abstract `SymbolicCost` shape — this file's lens
//   output) × (target-specific concrete cost — Rust-side composition
//   consumer). Concrete-cost wiring lives Rust-side per ε; this file's
//   substrate role does NOT change. T-CostLens follow-on multi-slice plan
//   (#2141 ε scope per gunbc#2068 #issuecomment-4402339074) sequences
//   gates #37 + #40 + #70 across separate PRs: Slice 1a.0/1a.1 staged
//   declaration lookup and .dag-tier meta resolvers; Slice 1a.2 adds the
//   Rust-side `RealizationCostTable` row walker over structural
//   `*Realization.cost` fields; Slice 1b parameterizes the concrete
//   cost-fold consumer → Slice 2 test_runner #40 wiring → Slice 3 demo
//   fixture #70. Those gates remain target-realization composition work
//   outside this lens's target-agnostic abstract `SymbolicCost` scope.
// See docs/v3-lens-capability-register.md.
//
// Produces `Witness<SymbolicCost>` facts per port using `SymbolicCost`
// combinators (`sequential`, `iterate`, `max_path`) from
// `std.algebra`, whose `SizeVariable` carrier is `source_port: PortId` +
// `display_name: String?` (presentation-only label; identity is `source_port`
// per `size_variable_eq`). This lens's fold usually builds variables via
// `unnamed_size_variable` / `linear_at`-style paths, so `display_name` is often
// `None` until producers author labels — unlike v2's richer `SizeVar` value
// semantics. Output dimensions, certainty, and asymptotic classification from
// v2's complexity analysis live on `complexity.dag`; this lens owns the abstract
// `SymbolicCost` projection. Executable Dimension wiring exists through
// `v3_compiler::analyze_symbolic_cost_dimension`, which returns
// `DimensionReport<SymbolicCost>` over this generated `symbolic_cost_of`
// authority. Lane E-C stages `CallPattern` /
// `LoweringTarget` in `std.computation`; lane E-I stages `SubValueRelation`
// and the `CostBound` algebra in `std.induction`. Integer **`Div`** composes
// operand costs (`transform_cost`) with **`LogCost(dividend_port)`** in
// `transform_cost_for_target`; other primitives still use input-port sum only.
// Recursive callable transforms consume per-call descent facts via
// `std.computation::per_call_pattern_at` (R3 gate `e_p_sub_value_relation_per_call_landed` /
// T-E-P-Producer-Broadening Phase 3): same `SubValueRelation`→`CallPattern` projection
// authority as `complexity.dag`, per `docs/design-cost-lens-sizevar-dimension-wiring.md` §3.2.
// Band-C cementing for the abstract cost projection lives at
// `integration/cementing/cost_lens_symbolic_consumer_test.rs`. E-M closed method
// carrier parity by structural subsumption
// through `TransformTarget` and typed declaration/effect metadata. Integration module
// `cost_lens_symbolic_consumer_test` pins the generated `symbolic_cost_of` consumer on
// `compile_to_dag` fixtures.
//
// Gate #104 (R3 §1.8): folded costs use `Witness<SymbolicCost>` end-to-end
// (`Inhabits` / `Violates { reason, at }`). Port-only callers use `symbolic_cost_of`
// with `resolve_producer` for attribution; lens read pins `Lens.read` attribution
// to the passed `Behavior` via `cost_lens_read`.

module lenses.cost

import std.list { List, empty, fold, cons }
import std.substrate {
  Dag, Behavior, BranchPath, LoopNode, LoopBound, NodeId, PortId, node,
  TransformNode, TransformTarget, OperatorKind, ArithmeticOp,
  resolve_producer
}
import std.algebra {
  MethodContract,
  CostShape,
  Monoid,
  SymbolicCost,
  dominates,
  unnamed_size_variable,
  sequential,
  iterate,
  max_path
}
import std.computation {
  CallPattern,
  ArithmeticSubtractCall,
  ArithmeticDivideCall,
  ChildAccessorCall,
  CollectionShrinkCall,
  FoldBodyCall,
  ParserAdvanceCall,
  WorklistDrainCall,
  SameArgumentCall,
  per_call_pattern_at,
  per_call_descent_operand_port
}
import v3.std.substrate { SourceSpan }
import v3.std.dimensions { Witness, OptionalDiagnostic }
import v3.std.lens { Lens }
import v3.std.lens_application { SectionRef, LensEnforcement, EnforceableLens }

// Cost-lens-owned user cost basis (T-User-Authored-Cost-Basis-Discipline audit:
// `docs/audit/t-user-authored-cost-basis-discipline-worked-examples.md`).
// Split from `EnforcedApplication` / `apply_lens` config: the latter owns enforcement
// mode + declared budget; these carriers attach evidence consumed when composing
// per-target costs (§4.2 PerWrite CRDT, §4.3 memory peak).
//
// Coproduct dissolution (`docs/modeling-discipline.md` §4). `CostBasisKind` classifies
// **which basis axis** cost evidence is keyed to (per write / per call / peak memory).
// **Mixed classification:** `PerWrite` and `PerCall` are **🟢 TERMINAL (GREEN)** evidence
// labels at the lens boundary; `PeakMemory` is **🟡 SCAFFOLD** until the peak-memory
// composition consumer + demo receipt land (ROADMAP / **#1954**, sibling to gate #93).
// Four-pattern ledger (terminal pair) — each pattern
// considered; none yields a cheaper substrate factoring without erasing audit vocabulary:
//   1. Fact placement — Fails as full dissolution: `PerWrite`, `PerCall`, and
//      `PeakMemory` are not redundant copies of the same fact at unrelated sites;
//      they are distinct basis kinds authors attach to the same `CostBasisDeclaration`
//      shell. Splitting into three unrelated carriers would triple `subject`/`cost`/`span`
//      payloads and scatter the cost-lens-owned “basis” concept the audit locks.
//   2. Variant-is-data — Rejected for modeling fidelity: the label space is closed
//      (three variants), but collapsing to a bare tag on a generic record would drop
//      the nominal tie to §4.2 / §4.3 / per-call surfaces in review and ROADMAP gates
//      (`crdt_cost_basis_demonstrated`, memory-peak sibling) — the variants are the
//      authored audit vocabulary, not an implementation detail.
//   3. Algebraic form — Fails: basis kinds are not references into a single `std/`
//      operator or algebra stem; they are evidence-class tags at the lens boundary.
//   4. Dimensional — Fails cleanly: peak-memory is not a product of the same axes as
//      per-write vs per-call (time/invocation structure vs allocation bound); merging
//      into one Cartesian record would conflate orthogonal enforcement stories.
//   5. **PeakMemory consumer — 🟡 SCAFFOLD:** unlike `PerWrite` (gate **#93** /
//      `try_build_per_write_log_cost_basis_declaration` + lens-table witnesses), there is
//      **no** Rust-side materializer or `compute_symbolic_costs` fold branch keyed on
//      `PeakMemory` yet. Authors may record the **label** for §4.3 / #1954 alignment; **P5:**
//      do not treat `PeakMemory` `CostBasisDeclaration` as enforcement-complete substrate
//      until **#1954** closes with a named consumer (same dissolution style as pre-`apply_lens`
//      CRDT staging).
//
// **Named dissolution trigger:** **#1954** (memory-peak cost-basis demo / composition consumer);
// `PerWrite` / `PerCall` labels need no separate trigger beyond their gate receipts.
type CostBasisKind
  = PerWrite
  | PerCall
  // 🟡 SCAFFOLD (#1954): `PeakMemory` — not a live terminal; see ledger §5 / block comment above (P5).
  | PeakMemory

// **Rust consumer (gate #93 / P2):** `v3_compiler::try_build_per_write_log_cost_basis_declaration`
// materializes **`PerWrite`** + `LogCost` evidence from post-lower `Dag` facts until class-5
// bodies persist `data` rows and the cost fold reads them into `compute_symbolic_costs`.
// **`PeakMemory`:** scaffold — consumer TBD per ledger §5 above (`#1954`).

// `subject` is `SectionRef` (`v3.std.lens_application`; design
// `docs/design-lens-application-surface.md` §2 — same structural authority as
// `EnforcedApplication.section`), not a bare `DeclarationId`, so expression-scoped
// bases can use `NodeScope` when landed.
type CostBasisDeclaration {
  subject: SectionRef
  kind: CostBasisKind
  cost: SymbolicCost
  span: SourceSpan
}

type SymbolicCostEntry {
  port: PortId
  cost: Witness<SymbolicCost>
}

fn lookup_cost_with_subject(
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  port_id: PortId,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  match acc {
    Empty =>
      Violates {
        reason: "symbolic_cost_of: missing SymbolicCost for behavior result port"
        at: subject
      }
    Cons(payload) =>
      if payload.head.port == port_id then
        payload.head.cost
      else
        lookup_cost_with_subject(payload.tail, port_id, subject)
  }

fn symbolic_cost_of(d: Dag, port_id: PortId) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  match resolve_producer(d, port_id) {
    Some(subject) =>
      lookup_cost_with_subject(
        compute_symbolic_costs(d),
        port_id,
        subject
      )
    None =>
      // INVARIANTS P1/P3: absent producer — no fabricated `Witness::Violates { at }` on an
      // unrelated node; advertise conservative lattice-top carrier only (PR #3137 review).
      wc_inhabits(
        UnknownCost("symbolic_cost_of: unresolved producer for port")
      )
  }

fn wc_inhabits(cost: SymbolicCost) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  Inhabits(cost)

fn witness_combine_sequential(
  wa: Witness<SymbolicCost>,
  wb: Witness<SymbolicCost>
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  match wa {
    Inhabits(ax) =>
      match wb {
        Inhabits(bx) => wc_inhabits(sequential(ax, bx))
        Violates { reason: rbody, at: abody } =>
          Violates {
            reason: rbody
            at: abody
          }
      }
    Violates { reason: rax, at: aax } =>
      Violates {
        reason: rax
        at: aax
      }
  }

fn witness_combine_iterate(
  bound_w: Witness<SymbolicCost>,
  body_w: Witness<SymbolicCost>
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  match bound_w {
    Inhabits(b) =>
      match body_w {
        Inhabits(y) => wc_inhabits(iterate(b, y))
        Violates { reason: ry, at: ay } =>
          Violates {
            reason: ry
            at: ay
          }
      }
    Violates { reason: rx, at: ax } =>
      Violates {
        reason: rx
        at: ax
      }
  }

fn witness_combine_max(
  wa: Witness<SymbolicCost>,
  wb: Witness<SymbolicCost>
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  match wa {
    Inhabits(ax) =>
      match wb {
        Inhabits(bx) => wc_inhabits(dominant(ax, bx))
        Violates { reason: r2, at: a2 } =>
          Violates {
            reason: r2
            at: a2
          }
      }
    Violates { reason: r1, at: a1 } =>
      Violates {
        reason: r1
        at: a1
      }
  }

// §6a Option 3 demo consumer: cost analysis reads per-method metadata from
// the unified carrier keyed by `(algebra_id, method_id)`, keeping the
// cost/size/callback facts co-located for later live call-site wiring.
fn method_contract_cost_shape(contract: MethodContract) -> CostShape? =
  contract.cost_shape

fn compute_symbolic_costs(d: Dag) -> List<SymbolicCostEntry> =
  fold(d.nodes, seed_bind_params(d.nodes), |acc, behavior|
    cons(entry_for(d, acc, behavior), acc)
  )

fn seed_bind_params(nodes: List<Behavior>) -> List<SymbolicCostEntry> =
  match nodes {
    Empty => empty()
    Cons(payload) =>
      concat_entries(params_of(payload.head), seed_bind_params(payload.tail))
  }

fn params_of(behavior: Behavior) -> List<SymbolicCostEntry> =
  match behavior {
    Value(v) => empty()
    Transform(t) => empty()
    Branch(b) => empty()
    Loop(l) => empty()
    Bind(bind) => param_entries(bind.params, behavior)
  }

fn param_entries(params: List<PortId>, subject: Behavior) -> List<SymbolicCostEntry> =
  match params {
    Empty => empty()
    Cons(payload) =>
      cons(
        { port: payload.head, cost: wc_inhabits(ConstantCost(0)) },
        param_entries(payload.tail, subject)
      )
  }

fn concat_entries(
  a: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  b: List<SymbolicCostEntry>
) -> List<SymbolicCostEntry> =
  match a {
    Empty => b
    Cons(payload) => cons(payload.head, concat_entries(payload.tail, b))
  }

fn entry_for(
  d: Dag,
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  behavior: Behavior
) -> SymbolicCostEntry =
  match behavior {
    Value(v) =>
      { port: v.result_port, cost: wc_inhabits(ConstantCost(0)) }
    Transform(t) =>
      match per_call_pattern_at(d, t.id) {
        None =>
          {
            port: t.result_port,
            cost: transform_cost_for_target(acc, t.target, t.inputs, behavior)
          }
        Some(pattern) =>
          match per_call_descent_operand_port(d, t.id) {
            None =>
              {
                port: t.result_port,
                cost: Violates {
                  reason: "symbolic_cost_of: recurrence descent operand unavailable for call pattern"
                  at: behavior
                }
              }
            Some(descent_port) =>
              {
                port: t.result_port,
                cost: recursive_transform_cost(
                  acc,
                  pattern,
                  descent_port,
                  t.inputs,
                  behavior
                )
              }
          }
      }
    Branch(b) =>
      {
        port: b.result_port,
        cost: branch_cost(acc, b.input, b.paths, behavior)
      }
    Loop(l) =>
      {
        port: l.result_port,
        cost: loop_cost(d, acc, l, behavior)
      }
    Bind(bind) =>
      {
        port: bind.result_port,
        cost: lookup_cost_with_subject(acc, bind.result_port, behavior)
      }
  }

// Recurrence iteration bound × operand spine from `inputs`, keyed by the same
// `per_call_pattern_at` projection over `SubValueRelation` evidence.
//
// Gate #104: recurrence body composes `Witness<SymbolicCost>` only (no `Lookup<>`).
fn recursive_transform_cost(
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  pattern: CallPattern,
  descent_port: PortId,
  inputs: List<PortId>,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  match inputs {
    Empty =>
      Violates {
        reason: "symbolic_cost_of: recursive callable transform expects operand ports"
        at: subject
      }
    Cons(_) =>
      witness_combine_iterate(
        pattern_to_iter_bound(pattern, descent_port, subject),
        witness_combine_sequential(
          lookup_cost_with_subject(acc, descent_port, subject),
          sum_costs_excluding_descent_operand(acc, inputs, descent_port, subject)
        )
      )
  }

// `SameArgumentCall` has no recurrence bound here — `Witness::Violates` (not `UnknownCost`).
fn pattern_to_iter_bound(
  pattern: CallPattern,
  arg_port: PortId,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  match pattern {
    ArithmeticSubtractCall { steps: steps, ring_param: ring_param } =>
      wc_inhabits(LinearCost(unnamed_size_variable(arg_port)))
    ArithmeticDivideCall { divisor: divisor , ring_param: ring_param } =>
      wc_inhabits(LogCost(unnamed_size_variable(arg_port)))
    ChildAccessorCall { accessor: accessor } =>
      wc_inhabits(LinearCost(unnamed_size_variable(arg_port)))
    CollectionShrinkCall { amount: amount, collection: collection } =>
      wc_inhabits(LinearCost(unnamed_size_variable(arg_port)))
    FoldBodyCall { outer_collection: outer_collection } =>
      wc_inhabits(LinearCost(unnamed_size_variable(arg_port)))
    ParserAdvanceCall { witness: witness } =>
      wc_inhabits(LinearCost(unnamed_size_variable(arg_port)))
    WorklistDrainCall { element: element } =>
      wc_inhabits(LinearCost(unnamed_size_variable(arg_port)))
    SameArgumentCall =>
      Violates {
        reason: "symbolic_cost_of: SameArgumentCall has no iterative recurrence bound"
        at: subject
      }
  }

fn loop_cost(
  d: Dag,
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  l: LoopNode,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  witness_combine_iterate(
    linear_at(l.source),
    body_cost(d, acc, l.body, subject)
  )

fn body_cost(
  d: Dag,
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  body_id: NodeId,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  match node(d, body_id) {
    None =>
      Violates {
        reason: "symbolic_cost_of: loop body node missing from Dag"
        at: subject
      }
    Some(body_behavior) =>
      lookup_cost_with_subject(acc, behavior_result_port(body_behavior), subject)
  }

fn behavior_result_port(b: Behavior) -> PortId =
  match b {
    Value(v) => v.result_port
    Transform(t) => t.result_port
    Branch(br) => br.result_port
    Loop(lp) => lp.result_port
    Bind(bind) => bind.result_port
  }

fn linear_at(port_id: PortId) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  wc_inhabits(LinearCost(unnamed_size_variable(port_id)))

fn branch_cost(
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  input: PortId,
  paths: List<BranchPath>,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  witness_combine_sequential(
    wc_inhabits(ConstantCost(1)),
    witness_combine_sequential(
      lookup_cost_with_subject(acc, input, subject),
      max_of_paths(acc, paths, subject)
    )
  )

fn max_of_paths(
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  paths: List<BranchPath>,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  fold(paths, wc_inhabits(ConstantCost(0)), |running, path|
    witness_combine_max(
      running,
      lookup_cost_with_subject(acc, path.result_port, subject)
    )
  )

// **Gate #94 (memory_peak_cost_basis_demonstrated):** same dominance-max lattice ...

fn dominant(a: SymbolicCost, b: SymbolicCost) -> SymbolicCost =
  max_path(cons(a, cons(b, empty())))

fn transform_cost_for_target(
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  target: TransformTarget,
  inputs: List<PortId>,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  match target {
    Callable(_) => transform_cost(acc, inputs, subject)
    UnresolvedFieldProject { field_label: l } => transform_cost(acc, inputs, subject)
    ResolvedFieldProject { field_label: f } => transform_cost(acc, inputs, subject)
    Operator(op) =>
      match op {
        Arithmetic(arith) =>
          match arith {
            Div =>
              match inputs {
                Cons(payload) =>
                  witness_combine_sequential(
                    transform_cost(acc, inputs, subject),
                    wc_inhabits(LogCost(unnamed_size_variable(payload.head)))
                  )
                Empty =>
                  Violates {
                    reason: "symbolic_cost_of: divide transform missing dividend port"
                    at: subject
                  }
              }
            Add => transform_cost(acc, inputs, subject)
            Sub => transform_cost(acc, inputs, subject)
            Mul => transform_cost(acc, inputs, subject)
          }
        Comparison(_) => transform_cost(acc, inputs, subject)
        Logical(_) => transform_cost(acc, inputs, subject)
      }
  }

fn transform_cost(
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  inputs: List<PortId>,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  witness_combine_sequential(
    wc_inhabits(ConstantCost(1)),
    sum_costs(acc, inputs, subject)
  )

fn sum_costs(
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  ports: List<PortId>,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  fold(ports, wc_inhabits(ConstantCost(0)), |running, port_id|
    witness_combine_sequential(
      running,
      lookup_cost_with_subject(acc, port_id, subject)
    )
  )

fn sum_costs_excluding_descent_operand(
  acc: List<SymbolicCostEntry>,
  ports: List<PortId>,
  descent_port: PortId,
  subject: Behavior
) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  fold(ports, wc_inhabits(ConstantCost(0)), |running, port_id|
    if port_id == descent_port then
      running
    else
      witness_combine_sequential(
        running,
        lookup_cost_with_subject(acc, port_id, subject)
      )
  )

// ── T-LAS Slice B — `Lens<SymbolicCost>` + canonical enforcement (gate #90) ──

fn cost_lens_read(d: Dag, b: Behavior) -> Witness<SymbolicCost> =
  lookup_cost_with_subject(
    compute_symbolic_costs(d),
    behavior_result_port(b),
    b
  )

fn cost_lens_sequential_op(a: SymbolicCost, b: SymbolicCost) -> SymbolicCost =
  sequential(a, b)

fn cost_lens_branch_op(a: SymbolicCost, b: SymbolicCost) -> SymbolicCost =
  dominant(a, b)

fn cost_lens_iterate_op(body: SymbolicCost, bound: LoopBound) -> SymbolicCost =
  match bound {
    Cardinality(payload) =>
      iterate(
        LinearCost(unnamed_size_variable(payload.count)),
        body
      )
    Descent(payload) =>
      iterate(
        LinearCost(unnamed_size_variable(payload.measure)),
        body
      )
  }

fn cost_lens_validate(d: Dag, c: SymbolicCost) -> OptionalDiagnostic =
  NoDiagnostic

fn cost_enforcement_project(c: SymbolicCost) -> SymbolicCost =
  c

// Strict excess in the `SymbolicCost` dominance lattice (mirrors
// `complexity_enforcement_violates` orientation vs `asymptotic_dominates`).
fn cost_enforcement_violates(observed: SymbolicCost, declared: SymbolicCost) -> Bool =
  if dominates(observed, declared) then
    if dominates(declared, observed) then 0 == 1 else 0 == 0
  else
    0 == 1

data cost_lens_monoid: Monoid<SymbolicCost> = {
  op: cost_lens_sequential_op
  identity: ConstantCost(0)
}

data cost_lens: Lens<SymbolicCost> = {
  name: "symbolic_cost"
  read: cost_lens_read
  sequential: cost_lens_monoid
  branch: cost_lens_branch_op
  iterate: cost_lens_iterate_op
  validate: cost_lens_validate
}

data cost_enforcement: LensEnforcement<SymbolicCost, SymbolicCost, SymbolicCost> = {
  project: cost_enforcement_project
  violates: cost_enforcement_violates
}

data cost_enforceable: EnforceableLens<SymbolicCost, SymbolicCost, SymbolicCost> = {
  lens: cost_lens
  enforcement: cost_enforcement
}

// ── T-CostLens-Composition α-narrow disposition (gunb-ai/gunbc#2141) ─
//
// **Director-ratified α (narrow)** at gunbc#828 #issuecomment-4400772335
// (relay: gunbc#2068 #issuecomment-4401002201). β (parallel-API) rejected
// per `feedback_isomorphism_or_generation_for_mirrors`; γ-extended
// (`Lens<C>.read` refactor) deferred to its own Q-Lens-Target-Context
// PROPOSAL canvas — NOT a T-CostLens stowaway.
//
// **Same-slice closure (PR #2171 receipts)**:
//   - **#38 `coercion_cost_equals_complexity_by_construction`** —
//     SATISFIED-BY-CONSTRUCTION at HEAD. `Semiring<SymbolicCost>`
//     `sequential` / `iterate` (`src/v3/std/algebra.dag:181-188`) is the
//     sole composition authority; no parallel "complexity-vs-cost"
//     reconciliation surface exists.
//   - **#39 `no_coercion_cost_dimension`** — SATISFIED-BY-CONSTRUCTION
//     at HEAD. `SymbolicCost` 7-variant (`std/algebra.dag:181`) is the
//     sole cost dimension; no parallel `CoercionCost` carrier exists per
//     grep across `src/v3/{std,lenses,spec}/`.
//
// **Deferred to follow-on canvas (gunb-ai/gunbc#2175)** —
// cross-cutting Behavior→primitive-identity wiring substrate:
//   - **#37** `cost_lens_reads_target_realization`
//   - **#40** `symbolic_cost_expr_equals_executable` (also Verification
//     Mgr lane #2075)
//   - **#70** `cost_lens_demonstration`
//
// Structural findings forcing the canvas-tier deferral (surfaced
// gunbc#2068 #issuecomment-4399898495 + #issuecomment-4400390687):
//   1. ~~No `data cost_lens` row~~ — **superseded at HEAD**: T-LAS Slice B
//      (`gate #90 lens_enforcement_carrier_landed`) lands `cost_lens` /
//      `cost_enforceable` as thin packaging over `symbolic_cost_of` above.
//      Target-context / richer iterate semantics remain under gunbc#2175.
//   2. `Lens<C>.read: fn(Dag, Behavior) -> Witness<C>` carries no
//      target-context — Q-Lens-Target-Context PROPOSAL territory.
//   3. Behavior→primitive-identity is structurally tractable via
//      `TransformNode.target: TransformTarget` (`Callable(DeclarationId)`,
//      `std/substrate.dag:418`) for Transform behaviors; other variants
//      need their own anchors.
//   4. `.dag`-side iteration over `List<CallableRealization>` /
//      `List<TypeRealization>` has zero precedent at HEAD; realizations
//      consumed Rust-side at emit time only. Introducing such iteration
//      is canvas-tier (#2175).
//
// ── Dimension<SymbolicCost> wiring — DEFERRED (class-5 data bodies) ─
//
// **Stage 2f dispatch (landed):** `v3_compiler::analyze_symbolic_cost_dimension`
// packages the same `symbolic_cost_of` / `compute_symbolic_costs` algebra as a
// `DimensionReport<SymbolicCost>` (DB-3). The `data symbolic_cost_dimension:
// Dimension<SymbolicCost> = { ... }` **value** remains blocked on record bodies;
// the Rust entrypoint is the interim authority — same pattern as ROADMAP §Lane 2.
//
// ── Dimension<SymbolicCost> data declaration — DEFERRED to class-5 ─
//
// DB-7 §"Dimension<SymbolicCost> wiring" specifies a
// `data symbolic_cost_dimension: Dimension<SymbolicCost> = {..}`
// declaration with `witness_of`, `compose`, `identity` fields
// carrying function references.
//
// Stage 2d does NOT ship this data declaration because v3's
// current parser/lowerer rejects two v3 surface-grammar gaps that
// the declaration's shape requires simultaneously:
//
//   1. Record literals inside `data X: T = { ... }` bodies. At
//      M1(2.8) the lowerer reports "data has an opaque body —
//      user code cannot yet use record / list / map literals
//      inside data bodies" (DOWNSTREAM_REQUIREMENTS.md class-5
//      gap #3).
//   2. Record literals / match / lambdas inside `fn X { body }`
//      block-bodied definitions. Constructing `Witness::Violates
//      { reason, at }` — the MissingCost-to-violation shim the
//      Dimension contract requires — hits the same block-body
//      restriction.
//
// The lens ships its Behavior-variant lowering (`entry_for` +
// helpers) as the authority. When Stage 2f's generic `analyze`
// walker lands, it will materialize the `Dimension<SymbolicCost>`
// instance alongside the surface-grammar extensions that unlock
// the receipt form. Dispatching the instance from here today
// would either require a parallel Rust-side declaration (bypassing
// `.dag`-as-authority) or wait on the grammar extension — the
// second path is the one the ROADMAP already sequences (Stage 2f
// extracts the abstraction once multiple instances exist).
//
// See `docs/design-symbolic-cost-algebra.md` §"Dimension<SymbolicCost>
// wiring" for the target shape.

// ── Cost dimension data declaration / forward Lens boundary ─
//
// Live target today is DB-3 / DB-7's analysis-dimension path:
//
//   data symbolic_cost_dimension: AnalysisDimension<SymbolicCost> = {
//     name: "symbolic_cost",
//     witness_of: symbolic_cost_witness_of,
//     compose: sequential,
//     identity: ConstantCost(0),
//     break_diagnostic: symbolic_cost_break_diagnostic
//   }
//
// Do NOT author that data value until class-5 data-body lowering can
// express the record honestly: function-valued field references,
// nested structural values, and the `Witness<SymbolicCost>` /
// `OptionalDiagnostic` constructors needed by `witness_of` and
// `break_diagnostic`. The current Rust entrypoint
// `v3_compiler::analyze_symbolic_cost_dimension` remains the execution
// authority over the same `DimensionReport<SymbolicCost>` carrier.
//
// This DB-3 path keeps symbolic-cost analysis at the Behavior /
// LoopNode boundary. A Loop witness may read `l.source`, `l.bound`, and
// the loop body through the Dag, so `LoopBound::Descent` is not by
// itself a blocker for the live `AnalysisDimension<SymbolicCost>`
// declaration. The existing `loop_cost(d, acc, l)` implementation keeps
// using `linear_at(l.source)` for both Cardinality and Descent loops
// until a richer, authoritative cluster-measure fact is introduced.
//
// Forward Lens<SymbolicCost> note: current cost semantics still read
// `LoopNode.source`, but R3 cost-lens composition should not carry that
// shortcut forward. `LoopBound::Descent` now carries its own runtime
// `measure: PortId`, plus the shared `loop_bound_measure(LoopBound) ->
// PortId` accessor, so a source-less `Lens<C>.iterate: fn(C, LoopBound)
// -> C` can read the bound honestly once the lens fold lands. Current
// mapping:
//
//   - `Cardinality { count }` -> `LinearCost({ source_port: count })`
//   - `Descent { cluster, measure }` -> currently
//     `LinearCost({ source_port: l.source })` through the enclosing
//     `LoopNode`, with a ratchet that `l.source ==
//     loop_bound_measure(l.bound)` until direct `LoopNode.source` cost
//     reads retire. The cluster sidecar carries termination witness
//     topology, not a replacement cost carrier.
//
// Do not choose `UnknownCost("mutual recursion descent cluster")` as a
// local migration convenience. `UnknownCost` is an algebra top, not a
// failure channel; if a future lens fold wants a different Descent cost
// policy, that must be named as the authoritative substrate decision.
// Until the class-5 data declaration and direct `LoopNode.source` cost
// reads retire, preserve `compute_symbolic_costs` / `symbolic_cost_of`
// as the primary API — `cost_lens` composes from those helpers (gate #90),
// not a divergent cost pipeline.
